public inherited sharing class AccountRatingService {

    private static final String RATING_HOT = 'Hot';
    private static final String RATING_WARM = 'Warm';
    private static final String RATING_COLD = 'Cold';
    private static final Decimal HOT_THRESHOLD = 100000;

    /**
     * Recalculates the Rating of the given accounts based on their open pipeline.
     * Runs asynchronously so opportunity DML stays fast. Call this once per
     * transaction with the full set of affected AccountIds (bulk-safe).
     */
    @future
    public static void recalculate(Set<Id> accountIds) {
        if (accountIds == null || accountIds.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        // accountId -> does it have an open opp >= threshold?
        Map<Id, Boolean> hasBigOpenOpp = new Map<Id, Boolean>();
        // accountId -> does it have any open opp?
        Map<Id, Boolean> hasOpenOpp = new Map<Id, Boolean>();
        for (Id accountId : accountIds) {
            hasBigOpenOpp.put(accountId, false);
            hasOpenOpp.put(accountId, false);
        }

        // Closed-won/lost/closed stages; "open" is anything where IsClosed = false.
        List<Opportunity> openOpps = [
            SELECT AccountId, Amount
            FROM Opportunity
            WHERE AccountId IN :accountIds
              AND IsClosed = false
        ];

        for (Opportunity opp : openOpps) {
            hasOpenOpp.put(opp.AccountId, true);
            if (opp.Amount != null && opp.Amount >= HOT_THRESHOLD) {
                hasBigOpenOpp.put(opp.AccountId, true);
            }
        }

        List<Account> accountsToUpdate = new List<Account>();
        for (Id accountId : accountIds) {
            String newRating;
            if (hasBigOpenOpp.get(accountId)) {
                newRating = RATING_HOT;
            } else if (hasOpenOpp.get(accountId)) {
                newRating = RATING_WARM;
            } else {
                newRating = RATING_COLD;
            }
            accountsToUpdate.add(new Account(Id = accountId, Rating = newRating));
        }

        // No cross-object trigger recursion risk: Account triggers are not in scope,
        // but an update that doesn't change Rating is skipped anyway.
        List<Account> changed = new List<Account>();
        Map<Id, Account> existing = new Map<Id, Account>(
            [SELECT Id, Rating FROM Account WHERE Id IN :accountIds]
        );
        for (Account acc : accountsToUpdate) {
            Account current = existing.get(acc.Id);
            if (current == null || current.Rating != acc.Rating) {
                changed.add(acc);
            }
        }

        if (!changed.isEmpty()) {
            UPDATE changed;
        }
    }
}
```

Notes on the implementation:

- **`IsClosed = false`** defines "open" so custom closed stages work without hardcoding stage picklist values.
- **Only update Accounts whose `Rating` actually changed** — avoids unnecessary DML, recurring async churn, and potential recursion.
- **`inherited sharing` + field safety**: the query only reads `Id`, `Amount`, `StageName`-independent `IsClosed`, and writes `Rating` — nothing user-confidential; if you need record-level enforcement in the future context, switch to `with sharing` and re-filter by accessibility.
- If volume grows past what `@future` comfortably handles (100k/day per-day limits), a queueable with chaining or a scheduled batch sweep would be the next step, but `@future` matches the stated requirement.

